              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Upfront vs. Long-Term Cost: Asphalt usually costs roughly half as much upfront, while metal requires higher initial spending but can outlast two shingle roofs over several decades. As highlighted in Metal Roofing vs Shingles: Cost, Key Differences & Comparison , metal also sheds snow and reflects solar heat, though shingles can trap heat in cold weather.",
